3. COMPONENT BREAKDOWN & VALUE MATRIX
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
* Card 1: Endurance Peak ("Longest Run")
  - Accent Bar: Top Golden Diamond Edge border.
  - Core Metric: Absolute maximum career single-activity mile counter (.max()).
  - Context Label: Date tracking stamp showing when that run was completed.

* Card 2: Velocity Benchmark ("Fastest Mile")
  - Accent Bar: Top Amethyst Purple Edge border.
  - Core Metric: Pure record velocity split calculated out of your split files.
  - Context Label: Date tracking stamp showing your all-time fastest mile split.

* Card 3: Macro Volume Peak ("Max Annual Volume")
  - Accent Bar: Top Sapphire Blue Edge border.
  - Core Metric: Historical peak calendar year cumulative distance sum.
  - Context Label: Explicit year stamp (e.g., "Achieved in 2024").

* Card 4: Standard Course Split Desk ("Course PRs")
  - Accent Bar: Top Emerald Green Edge border.
  - Core Metric: Vertical stacked line list matching standard global distances.
  - Context Label: Clean timeline logs indicating your personal records across 
    the 5K, 10K, and Half Marathon tracks.

4. DYNAMIC LINK INTERACTION
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
* Every card is anchored back to your core dataset.
* Clicking on any record row or historical date token will immediately target
  the master database index and populate the exact run details inside the 
  Verification Drawer at the bottom of the screen. This allows you to inspect 
  the heart rate splits, cadence metrics, and conditions behind that lifetime best.
